.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1214 PM PDT Mon Sep 7 2026
(Wednesday through next Sunday)

Global ensemble clusters are in agreement that the ridge will be
tamped down by an upper-level low digging into the Pacific Northwest
Friday. This will kickoff the cooling trend with temperatures
moderating to near normal. The tightening of the pressure gradient
will bring an increase in onshore flow and strong northerly breezes
across the waters.

