.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1054 AM PDT Mon Sep 7 2026

Weak offshore aloft has resulted in VFR conditions across much of
the region. Onshore winds are forecast to increase this afternoon
and into the early evening before diminishing after sunset and more
so into Tuesday morning. Winds today are forecast to be weaker than
previous days however. Low confidence for stratus to return early
Tuesday morning with the greatest potential being around the
Monterey Bay terminals. Onshore winds return Tuesday by early
afternoon, yet may be delayed in timing.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. Light offshore flow persists at SFO this
morning, but is forecast to become west-northwesterly between 21Z-
23Z and prevail until late this evening. Winds ease into Tuesday
morning and become light/variable or offshore at times. There is low
confidence for stratus to return early Tuesday morning with
generally a 10-30% probability of reaching MVFR CIGs. Thus, have
left out of the official forecast at this time.

SFO Bridge Approach...The potential for MVFR CIGs Tuesday
morning is less than 10%. Otherwise, similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Currently variable winds at both
sites with increasing onshore winds between 19Z-20Z. Winds ease
late this evening after sunset and become light/variable early
Tuesday morning. There is a 20-40% probability for sub-VFR between
approximately 08Z-17Z, however confidence is not great enough to
include in the official forecast at this time. Once any low clouds
that do develop mixout, expecting VFR conditions to return by
around 17Z.

