.BEACHES...
Issued at 1213 AM PDT Mon Sep 7 2026

A Beach Hazards Statement is in effect through Labor Day. Moderate
to long period swell will increase the chance for sneaker waves,
since there are 2 different sets of southerly swell, and their
energy will periodically combine. In addition to sneaker waves,
expect strong rip currents and breaking waves up to 10 ft. As this
is a holiday weekend and the weather is otherwise pretty nice,
the exposure to the risk is high. Avoid the water if you`re not an
expert swimmer. If caught in a rip current, swim parallel to shore
until you stop feeling the pull. Even on the beach, be prepared
for sneaker waves this weekend and never turn your back on the
ocean.

